1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,311
Five thousand rupees a month

2
00:00:02,331 --> 00:00:03,864
can become fifty lakh.

3
00:00:03,884 --> 00:00:05,776
So why does your SIP feel

4
00:00:05,796 --> 00:00:06,633
useless?

5
00:00:06,653 --> 00:00:08,265
Say you invest five thousand

6
00:00:08,285 --> 00:00:09,448
rupees a month.

7
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:10,492
After five years,

8
00:00:10,512 --> 00:00:12,005
you've put in three lakh.

9
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:13,623
It's worth about four lakh.

10
00:00:13,643 --> 00:00:14,621
Feels slow.

11
00:00:14,641 --> 00:00:15,618
After ten years:

12
00:00:15,638 --> 00:00:16,405
six lakh in.

13
00:00:16,425 --> 00:00:17,927
About eleven and a half

14
00:00:17,947 --> 00:00:18,562
lakh.

15
00:00:18,582 --> 00:00:19,761
After twenty years:

16
00:00:19,781 --> 00:00:20,743
twelve lakh in.

17
00:00:20,763 --> 00:00:22,153
About fifty lakh.

18
00:00:22,173 --> 00:00:22,853
Same SIP.

19
00:00:22,873 --> 00:00:23,744
Same amount.

20
00:00:23,764 --> 00:00:25,653
The growth just shows up

21
00:00:25,673 --> 00:00:26,354
late.

22
00:00:26,374 --> 00:00:27,451
That's compounding.

23
00:00:27,471 --> 00:00:29,152
Your returns start earning

24
00:00:29,172 --> 00:00:30,624
their own returns.

25
00:00:30,644 --> 00:00:32,063
And most people quit in

26
00:00:32,083 --> 00:00:32,709
year three,

27
00:00:32,729 --> 00:00:34,716
right before the curve bends.

28
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:36,489
This assumes twelve percent

29
00:00:36,509 --> 00:00:36,988
a year.

30
00:00:37,008 --> 00:00:38,871
Real returns go up and down,

31
00:00:38,891 --> 00:00:40,853
and nothing is guaranteed.

32
00:00:40,873 --> 00:00:42,493
So don't judge your SIP

33
00:00:42,513 --> 00:00:43,371
by year one.

34
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:45,906
Judge it by year fifteen.
